steps.text:
**Answer: TJX beat its Q4 FY2025 pre-tax margin guidance by 75 basis points against the midpoint (70 bps against the top of the range).**

**Guidance:** In its Q3 FY2025 update, 
the retailer expects pretax profit margin for the fourth quarter of the fiscal to be in the range of 10.8% to 10.9%
. The midpoint is 10.85%.

**Actual result:** For the 13-week fourth quarter of Fiscal 2025, 
the Company's pretax profit margin was 11.6%
. The company said this was 
above the high-end of its plan by 0.7 percentage points, primarily driven by lower than expected inventory shrink expense as well as expense leverage on the above-plan sales, partially offset by higher incentive compensation accruals.


**Calculation:**
- Versus the midpoint: 11.60% − 10.85% = 0.75 percentage points = **+75 bps (beat)**
- Versus the top of the range: 11.60% − 10.90% = 0.70 percentage points = +70 bps (beat). This matches the company's own "0.7 percentage points" statement.

Either way, the result was a beat. The 75 bps figure is the headline because it uses the midpoint of the guided range.

